---
import Layout from "@/layouts/main.astro"

import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from "@/components/ui/card"
import { CsvWorkbench } from "@/components/csv-workbench"
---

<Layout
  title="FixMyImport | Clean, dedupe, and split import-ready CSVs"
  description="Fix messy CSV exports in your browser. Remove duplicates, split large files, and download import-ready batches with no upload and no account."
>
  <main class="w-full px-4 py-6 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <section id="tool" class="w-full">
      <CsvWorkbench client:load />
    </section>

    <section class="w-full pt-8">
      <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        <Card>
          <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>What This Tool Does</CardTitle>
          </CardHeader>
          <CardContent>
            <p>
              FixMyImport cleans messy CSVs, removes exact duplicates, splits
              large files into smaller batches, previews the output, and exports
              the result in one short browser session.
            </p>
          </CardContent>
        </Card>
        <Card>
          <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>Why It Starts Simple</CardTitle>
          </CardHeader>
          <CardContent>
            <p>
              The first screen focuses on the main workflow only. Cleanup,
              dedupe, and split details stay inside the advanced dialog until
              you actually need them.
            </p>
          </CardContent>
        </Card>
        <Card>
          <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>Who It Helps First</CardTitle>
          </CardHeader>
          <CardContent>
            <p>
              Shopify is the first sharp workflow, with presets for Excel,
              Mailchimp, HubSpot, and Salesforce style import prep already
              available.
            </p>
          </CardContent>
        </Card>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="w-full pt-8">
      <div class="grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <Card>
          <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>How It Works</CardTitle>
          </CardHeader>
          <CardContent className="space-y-3">
            <p>1. Load or paste a CSV.</p>
            <p>2. Start with an import preset.</p>
            <p>3. Review the cleaned preview and export plan.</p>
            <p>
              4. Open advanced rules only if the default output needs
              adjustment.
            </p>
            <p>5. Download one CSV or a ZIP of smaller batch files.</p>
          </CardContent>
        </Card>

        <Card>
          <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>Privacy And Processing</CardTitle>
          </CardHeader>
          <CardContent className="space-y-3">
            <p>
              The default workflow runs in the browser, so the CSV does not need
              to be uploaded to use the tool.
            </p>
            <p>
              The page is designed for quick import preparation rather than full
              spreadsheet editing, which keeps the workflow narrow and easier to
              understand.
            </p>
            <p>
              More detailed notes are available on the
              <a href="/privacy" class="underline underline-offset-4"
                >privacy page</a
              >.
            </p>
          </CardContent>
        </Card>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="w-full pt-8">
      <Card>
        <CardHeader>
          <CardTitle>FAQ</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent className="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <p class="font-medium">Does the file get uploaded?</p>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              No. The normal workflow is browser-first and local.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <p class="font-medium">Can I change the cleanup rules?</p>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              Yes. Open the advanced dialog to adjust cleaning, dedupe, and
              split settings.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <p class="font-medium">What if the CSV is too large?</p>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              The tool supports smaller batch exports, and the Pro unlock path
              is there for larger local exports.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <p class="font-medium">Which workflows are most supported?</p>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              Shopify is the first sharp workflow, with presets for other
              import-heavy tools already available.
            </p>
          </div>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>
    </section>

    <section class="w-full pt-8">
      <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        <Card>
          <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>About</CardTitle>
          </CardHeader>
          <CardContent>
            <p>
              FixMyImport is meant to be a narrow import-prep utility, not a
              spreadsheet replacement.
            </p>
          </CardContent>
        </Card>
        <Card>
          <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>Guides</CardTitle>
          </CardHeader>
          <CardContent className="space-y-2">
            <p>
              <a
                href="/shopify-csv-cleaner"
                class="underline underline-offset-4">Shopify import guide</a
              >
            </p>
            <p>
              <a
                href="/mailchimp-csv-too-large"
                class="underline underline-offset-4"
                >Mailchimp file-too-large guide</a
              >
            </p>
          </CardContent>
        </Card>
        <Card>
          <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>More Details</CardTitle>
          </CardHeader>
          <CardContent>
            <p>
              Privacy notes, workflow guidance, and supporting context live
              below the tool instead of blocking the first-use experience.
            </p>
          </CardContent>
        </Card>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
